1
00:00:03,230 --> 00:00:04,850
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,330 --> 00:00:10,630
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:14,460
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:17,470
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:21,510
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:03,040
O prince...

7
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:07,220
O prince of the unforgiven...

8
00:01:09,090 --> 00:01:12,530
We are honored to be received in audience...

9
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:29,810
We shall meet again in another world...

10
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:37,010
We are your kin...

11
00:02:02,470 --> 00:02:04,560
Feel no shame about shape

12
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,480
Weather changes their phrase

13
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,230
Even mother will show you another way

14
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:12,610
So put your glasses on

15
00:02:12,690 --> 00:02:14,690
Nothing will be wrong

16
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:16,900
There's no blame. There's no fame

17
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,740
It's up to you

18
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:22,370
The first words should be found

19
00:02:22,990 --> 00:02:26,000
Whatever holds you back

20
00:02:26,870 --> 00:02:27,370
I...

21
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:28,500
...can...

22
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:30,670
I can get it off

23
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:31,670
Tell me what...

24
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:32,670
Tell me what...

25
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:34,500
Tell me what you want

26
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:35,590
I don't know why...

27
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:36,590
Don't know why...

28
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:38,590
Don't know why you're afraid

29
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,760
Tell me what...

30
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,720
Tell me what...

31
00:02:40,890 --> 00:02:42,390
Tell me what you'd say

32
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:43,720
I don't know why...

33
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:44,810
Don't know why...

34
00:02:44,890 --> 00:02:45,600
Too late...

35
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,220
It's too late

36
00:02:52,150 --> 00:02:56,150
Infiltration

37
00:03:26,390 --> 00:03:30,350
Are you sure there's a secret
passage in this dismal place?

38
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,310
Our sources are reliable.

39
00:03:32,730 --> 00:03:36,820
If it's so easy to find, then who would
need the help of us mercenaries?

40
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:40,820
Found it.

41
00:03:42,610 --> 00:03:43,780
I guess we're not needed.

42
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:45,620
Pippin.

43
00:03:59,670 --> 00:04:01,050
There's no mistake.

44
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:01,760
This is it.

45
00:04:02,090 --> 00:04:03,470
Right, let's go.

46
00:04:03,470 --> 00:04:04,470
Wait a minute.

47
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:07,430
I understand that Pippin and
Judeau need to come along...

48
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:10,560
...but you're the commander now.
Are you sure you should come?

49
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,180
If something were to happen to you...

50
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:15,150
Our mission is to rescue Griffith.

51
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,310
We have the highest chance to succeed...

52
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:20,150
...if all four of our strongest
members take on the operation.

53
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,490
Yeah, but...

54
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,860
You're worried, aren't you?

55
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,660
Don't make me laugh!

56
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:29,700
I'm a stronger swordsman
than either of them.

57
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,210
Don't bring your personal
feelings into this matter.

58
00:04:33,210 --> 00:04:34,670
Obey your commander's orders!

59
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,210
Remember...

60
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:41,630
...I can still cover your back.

61
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:42,590
Don't forget that.

62
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:45,050
Yeah...

63
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:48,260
Let's go.

64
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:16,500
Griffith...

65
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:19,630
You were always looking up to the sky...

66
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:25,260
To climb higher... To soar higher...
That's all you wanted to do.

67
00:05:26,630 --> 00:05:29,680
You were a hawk flying alone,
reaching for the highest point...

68
00:05:31,810 --> 00:05:32,720
That's right...

69
00:05:33,270 --> 00:05:35,810
You were always watching us from above...

70
00:05:35,810 --> 00:05:37,730
Never here on the ground
with the rest of us...

71
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,480
Calm, cool, and always on the alert.

72
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:46,400
Do you really need a reason...

73
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:49,660
...each time I decide to lay
my life on the line for you?

74
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,870
Letting nothing stand
in your path to victory...

75
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:57,500
Do you find me vile?

76
00:06:00,290 --> 00:06:03,550
Griffith can't go on without you!

77
00:06:05,210 --> 00:06:06,630
If that's true...

78
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:08,680
If that's the real truth...

79
00:06:09,130 --> 00:06:10,220
Then I...

80
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:25,570
Pull yourself together.

81
00:06:25,570 --> 00:06:27,900
Griffith will be back soon.

82
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:30,360
There's no way in hell I'm going to die...

83
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,070
Not without seeing Griffith...

84
00:06:32,570 --> 00:06:35,540
Even if I need a thousand
more stitches in me...

85
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:38,830
Rickert, we need some more water.

86
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:39,670
Got it.

87
00:06:42,130 --> 00:06:44,290
When Griffith returns...

88
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:46,960
It'll be the resurrection
of the Band of the Hawk!

89
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:56,970
Everyone is in good spirits...

90
00:06:58,350 --> 00:07:00,980
Because Griffith will be back soon...

91
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:06,230
As long as Griffith comes back, then...

92
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:27,340
A fairy?

93
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:35,930
I saw it...

94
00:07:35,930 --> 00:07:38,560
...with my very own eyes.
There's no doubt.

95
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:47,020
The enemy?

96
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:48,360
Why now?

97
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,570
Just a little more...

98
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:55,280
All we needed was a little more time,
and Griffith would be back!

99
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,540
We can't let them destroy us! Not now!

100
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:12,380
Hey...

101
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,340
Where is everyone?

102
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,140
Run...

103
00:08:34,450 --> 00:08:35,410
Run...

104
00:08:36,910 --> 00:08:38,080
Rickert...

105
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:12,780
It can't...

106
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,950
This can't be real!

107
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:44,640
What...

108
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:46,440
What's going on?

109
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:02,700
I'm amazed we learned
about this secret passage.

110
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:03,990
We have supporters inside.

111
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:09,670
Wait.

112
00:10:10,330 --> 00:10:11,790
Supporters of the resistance movement...

113
00:10:18,970 --> 00:10:20,510
You must be the Band of the Hawk.

114
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:22,510
We are at your service.

115
00:10:22,510 --> 00:10:23,970
The Band of the Hawk's Casca.

116
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:26,350
What do you mean by supporters?

117
00:10:26,730 --> 00:10:28,730
They're from Princess Charlotte.

118
00:10:28,730 --> 00:10:29,440
Oh...

119
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:31,900
We don't have very much time until dawn.

120
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:35,820
We must get to where Griffith's
being kept as soon as possible.

121
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:36,650
Right.

122
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,010
We'll take it from here.

123
00:11:35,590 --> 00:11:39,760
Darkness... True darkness, where not
a single ray of light can be found.

124
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:45,680
How long have I been
lying here in this darkness?

125
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,060
An eternity...

126
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,600
...or perhaps a fleeting moment.

127
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:56,610
I feel nothing...

128
00:11:59,570 --> 00:12:02,400
It's as if my body is floating in space...

129
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:07,450
I wonder... Have I managed
to preserve my sanity?

130
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:12,120
Or has it already been lost long ago?

131
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:15,960
And yet...

132
00:12:16,590 --> 00:12:18,800
...here in this empty, hollow world...

133
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:21,670
...one thing is clear in my mind.

134
00:12:27,050 --> 00:12:28,390
Him alone...

135
00:12:28,890 --> 00:12:31,930
...like lightning splitting
through the darkness...

136
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:36,060
He appears in my mind so vividly.

137
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:42,490
Over and over again like
the waves of a tsunami...

138
00:12:43,070 --> 00:12:44,150
Hatred...

139
00:12:44,530 --> 00:12:45,490
Friendship...

140
00:12:46,030 --> 00:12:47,030
Jealousy...

141
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:48,780
Frustration...

142
00:12:49,330 --> 00:12:50,370
Helplessness...

143
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:52,120
Affection...

144
00:12:52,410 --> 00:12:53,460
Sorrow...

145
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:57,540
They all come together
into a giant vortex...

146
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:03,050
They pin my fading consciousness
down so that it doesn't slip away.

147
00:13:05,050 --> 00:13:10,430
The one who caused this...
My confinement in this darkness...

148
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,560
Will now...

149
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:15,890
...become my only chance at survival.

150
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:21,070
When did it happen? This man,
whose life was once in my hands...

151
00:13:21,570 --> 00:13:25,860
When did I fall into his powerful clutches?

152
00:13:28,990 --> 00:13:30,700
And now...

153
00:13:31,450 --> 00:13:36,040
In my mind I see him radiating
so brightly it pierces my eyes.

154
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:39,210
Guts!

155
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:52,470
Griffith?

156
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:54,930
Griffith?

157
00:13:56,230 --> 00:13:57,560
Is he in a different cell?

158
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:00,900
No, he has to be here on the lowest level.

159
00:14:12,490 --> 00:14:13,200
Griffith?

160
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:14,370
Grif...

161
00:14:21,210 --> 00:14:21,880
Gri...

162
00:14:22,590 --> 00:14:23,630
Griffith...

163
00:14:39,730 --> 00:14:42,770
The tendons in his arms
and legs have been slashed...

164
00:14:45,730 --> 00:14:46,820
And his tongue...

165
00:14:48,070 --> 00:14:49,400
Casca, the keys!

166
00:14:51,450 --> 00:14:52,030
Casca!

167
00:15:12,430 --> 00:15:13,510
Stay there!

168
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,220
Stay where you are!

169
00:15:18,430 --> 00:15:19,940
This isn't possible.

170
00:15:20,730 --> 00:15:24,110
This can't be Griffith...

171
00:15:39,410 --> 00:15:40,120
Guts...

172
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:42,040
Griffith!

173
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:30,630
There's no escaping now...

174
00:16:33,470 --> 00:16:37,510
The guards and soldiers
will be here any minute...

175
00:16:38,970 --> 00:16:43,640
And in a year, you'll all
be looking just like him...

176
00:16:46,230 --> 00:16:47,400
You bastard...

177
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:53,030
So you're the bastard
who destroyed his body...

178
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:55,070
That's right.

179
00:16:55,450 --> 00:16:58,450
I haven't had that
much fun in a long time.

180
00:16:58,450 --> 00:17:03,040
You don't come across a specimen
as splendid as him very often.

181
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:05,750
When you're as experienced as
I am in the profession of torture...

182
00:17:05,750 --> 00:17:08,420
...not only do you appreciate
the beauty that's on the surface...

183
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:14,010
...but also the beauty beneath the skin,
in the tendons, muscles, and veins.

184
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:17,680
He really was exquisite.

185
00:17:19,010 --> 00:17:20,310
It's no use.

186
00:17:20,310 --> 00:17:24,180
This door is four times
thicker than your average door.

187
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:48,080
Don't move!

188
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:49,750
Put down your weapons and surrender!

189
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:53,050
Stick with me and don't fall back!

190
00:17:54,170 --> 00:17:54,920
Guts!

191
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:07,850
How dare you?

192
00:18:07,850 --> 00:18:08,980
What the hell are you all doing?

193
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:09,900
Shoot them!

194
00:18:22,910 --> 00:18:24,120
You idiots!

195
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:25,200
Who said to retreat?

196
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,370
Hold your ground!

197
00:18:32,090 --> 00:18:32,920
Hurry!

198
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:35,670
What's taking them so long?

199
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:38,880
There are thirty of our soldiers
against just the four of them!

200
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,510
How can it be so difficult?

201
00:18:40,510 --> 00:18:42,140
Yes, but, sir...

202
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:45,010
...they're led by that man,
the hundred-man slayer!

203
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:46,310
Don't be stupid!

204
00:18:46,310 --> 00:18:50,270
How can we be sure that their
raider commander himself is here?

205
00:18:50,270 --> 00:18:51,230
No...

206
00:18:51,230 --> 00:18:55,110
Besides, myths like that
are born in times of war...

207
00:18:55,110 --> 00:18:58,240
...when stories get exaggerated.

208
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:04,160
There is no man in the world who
can slay a hundred armed soldiers.

209
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:07,120
Maybe ten soldiers at the very most.

210
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:22,050
That is definitely him...

211
00:19:22,050 --> 00:19:24,220
The Band of the Hawk's
ruthless commander...

212
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:24,930
Guts!

213
00:19:25,260 --> 00:19:27,060
It's Hundred-Man Guts himself!

214
00:19:30,190 --> 00:19:32,400
Surround him!
What are you waiting for?

215
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,860
Seize him!

216
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:34,650
But, sir...

217
00:19:35,020 --> 00:19:36,190
You idiots!

218
00:19:36,190 --> 00:19:40,950
He's been waving his huge sword
around while chasing after our men...

219
00:19:40,950 --> 00:19:43,030
He's out of breath.

220
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:45,490
You fools!

221
00:19:45,490 --> 00:19:50,750
If your enemy sees you hesitating,
you've already lost the battle.

222
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:55,460
Put your lives on the line and
see how ruthless the battlefield is!

223
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:00,220
Guts!

224
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,850
Advance!

225
00:20:12,890 --> 00:20:13,850
Where are they?

226
00:20:13,850 --> 00:20:15,690
See, it was too much
for just the four of them...

227
00:20:16,020 --> 00:20:16,860
No...

228
00:20:16,860 --> 00:20:18,360
You're wrong. They'll be back.

229
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:19,980
I'm sure of it.

230
00:20:33,250 --> 00:20:34,000
Guts...

231
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,920
What a disgrace!

232
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:20,130
If we let them get away,
the king will never forgive us.

233
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:22,090
Pursue them!

234
00:21:22,550 --> 00:21:25,130
We're going to head them off
and then ambush them!

235
00:21:25,130 --> 00:21:25,800
Yes, sir!

236
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

237
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

238
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

239
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

240
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

241
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

242
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

243
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

244
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

245
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

246
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

